      "words": 50
    },
    {
      "block": "原句2",
      "no": 2,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "Right. Okay. I have to take this notecard to the police. They can take fingerprints, or do forensics, or something",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 404
        },
        {
          "text": "I glance around for something to pick it up with, since using my bare hands isn’t possible. There’s a stack of cloth nap",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 648
        }
      ],
      "words": 70
    },
    {
      "block": "原句3",
      "no": 3,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "When I open the napkin over my purse, the card falls about an inch—only to rise back up again as if pulled by an invisib",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 905
        },
        {
          "text": "My eyes must be playing tricks on me",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 1050
        },
        {
          "text": "Once again the card floats back up to the napkin like gravity is nothing but some cosmic joke to it",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 1238
        }
      ],
      "words": 56
    },
    {
      "block": "原句4",
      "no": 4,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "The only person I can turn to right now is Jess. She’ll know from her nurse training whether I’m showing signs of someon",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 1730
        },
        {
          "text": "She starts responding again immediately. Like she’s been expecting this",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 2982
        },
        {
          "text": "But other than getting the reason for my freak-out wrong, my little sister has me pegged exactly right",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 3388
        }
      ],
      "words": 57
    },
    {
      "block": "原句5",
      "no": 5,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "For now, I try to wrangle my guilt into something smaller and more manageable. I need to keep it together at least until",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 3840
        },
        {
          "text": "I step into the intersection, my eyes glued to my phone as I wait for Jess’s next texts to appear",
          "ok": true,
